	(text "Link to the shack (D-56, D-57): Cat6 #1 UTP, four opto current loops, 10 mA each, powered from the shack (12 V, about 820R there).\nT568B pairs, + wire first: pair 1 = pins 4/5 data in, pair 2 = 1/2 PTT, pair 3 = 3/6 SAFE, pair 4 = 7/8 data out.\nEntry per pair: GDT to CHASSIS (box earth), common-mode choke L1 to L4 with Y-capacitor footprints to CHASSIS (not fitted, D-130),\n47R MELF per wire (loop current = voltage across it / 47R, the test access), SMBJ15CA across the pair; then the opto.\nReceive: loop current = LED on = output low. DATA_RX idle (mark) is low: the UART RX is inverted in firmware (ESP32-C3 line inverse).\nPTT: FT-710 TX GND closes loop 2; PTT_N low; U5 gives TX_ANY and the K0 drives, in hardware, not through the MCU.\nSAFE (D-62): loop 3 through the shack KILL switch and sense, and the box READY switch U6 (closed while NOR(MCU_EN_N, FAULT) = 1 and RF_A2_N = 1);\nRF_A2_N (D-104, SR-01 H2): RF board A2 detector, low = RF on the receive-only column: U16 opens READY, the shack inhibits all radios.\nany break (KILL, READY open, cut cable, no shack supply) = no current = KILL high (to the safety gate). R52, R53 not fitted (D-63).\nTransmit: DATA_TX high (UART idle) = LED on = loop closed; MCU off = loop open, so the shack sees a break. 9600 baud (C-18)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 259.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
